    <string name="network_guide_title">Developer &amp; Network Guide</string>
    <string name="network_guide_body">• Android Emulator: Use http://10.0.2.2:5000/api/v1 to reach localhost:5000 on your development machine.\n• Physical Device on LAN: Use your development machine\'s Wi-Fi IP address (e.g. http://192.168.1.50:5000/api/v1).\n• Production: Requires HTTPS (e.g. https://api.kidsguard.example.com/api/v1).\n• Insecure HTTP is permitted only for local loopback addresses (10.0.2.2, 127.0.0.1, localhost).</string>

    <string name="limitations_title">Platform Capabilities &amp; Limitations</string>
    <string name="limitations_body">• KidsGuard operates transparently using standard Android APIs.\n• Ordinary Android apps cannot unilaterally block or close other applications.\n• Cannot enforce a hard system shutdown or lock the child out of settings.\n• Cannot prevent app uninstallation on unmanaged devices without Android Enterprise / MDM.\n• Website domain restrictions are managed by parents on the web dashboard and enforced on desktop Chrome browsers via the KidsGuard Extension.</string>
